version: 0.1.0.1
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24128912"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: https://github.com/Fancryer/snapshots
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24128912
abstract: >-
  Mårran is an experimental statically typed programming language exploring the
  interaction between non-strict evaluation, controlled mutation and algebraic
  effects. A binding qualifier imm evaluates a delayed computation in a snapshot
  of the environment, in which data is copied and reachable code is frozen so
  that it neither creates nor observes mutable state. This artifact contains the
  implementation, the type-and-effect inference engine, the test suite, the
  Criterion benchmark harness and the Lean 4 development that accompanies the
  paper.
keywords:
  - programming languages
  - non-strict evaluation
  - mutable state
  - effect systems
  - snapshots
